{"timestamp": "2026-07-29T18:51:33.328926", "data": {"url": "https://esgsource.com/directory/bloomberg-esg", "title": "Bloomberg ESG | ESGsource", "content": "Skip to main content Data & Measurement \u00b7 Vendor Featured \u00b7 Private Bloomberg ESG Data Bloomberg, the financial information and news leader, provides integrated ESG data and analytics through its Bloomberg Terminal platform. Bloomberg ESG combines corporate sustainability disclosures, news coverage, and proprietary research to deliver ESG insights alongside traditional financial data. Bloomberg's ESG offering includes carbon emissions data, ESG risk scores across multiple methodologies, supply chain information, and governance metrics. The integration with the Bloomberg Terminal makes it a standard tool for institutional investors conducting ESG analysis and portfolio management. Bloomberg has also developed climate analytics tools including implied temperature rise calculations and scenario analysis capabilities. The platform supports compliance with TCFD , SFDR , EU Taxonomy , and other regulatory requirements. Its comprehensive ESG data, combined with fundamental market data, makes it an essential platform for large asset managers and investment banks. In short Bloomberg provides comprehensive ESG data, analytics, and research integrated into its Terminal platform, used by thousands of institutional investors globally. Best for Institutional investors needing integrated ESG data with comprehensive market data Section \u00b7 Catalog Products & Services Data & Analytics ESG Data Module Integrated ESG metrics and scores within Bloomberg Terminal Climate Analytics Carbon Analytics Emissions data, carbon footprint calculations, and climate scenario analysis Governance Governance Data Board composition, compensation, voting rights, and corporate governance metrics Supply Chain Supply Chain ESG Supply chain sustainability risk assessment and supplier ESG profiles Section \u00b7 Why this org Key strengths Integrated with Bloomberg Terminal \u2014 industry standard for institutional investors Comprehensive ESG data across multiple dimensions (environmental, social, governance) Strong news and controversy monitoring integrated with ESG metrics Advanced climate analytics and scenario modeling tools Section \u00b7 Use cases Where it\u2019s used Portfolio ESG screening and construction Regulatory compliance reporting (SFDR, EU Taxonomy) Climate risk assessment and scenario analysis Supply chain ESG due diligence Section \u00b7 Taxonomy Categories Data ESG Data & Ratings Data ESG Data Infrastructure Section \u00b7 Aligned with Related frameworks GRI standard GRI Standards SASB standard SASB Standards TCFD framework TCFD Recommendations ISSB standard ISSB Standards (IFRS S1 & S2) History & Timeline Founding, major releases, regulation, adoption, and evolution of Bloomberg ESG . In 2026 Last reviewed April 20, 2026 Bloomberg ESG data products continue expanding climate and transition analytics coverage Bloomberg's sustainability data offerings remain integrated with terminal and enterprise workflows in 2026, with continued emphasis on emissions, climate risk, and disclosure comparability datasets. 2026-01-30 Bloomberg continues distributing ESG and climate datasets through terminal and enterprise data products used by institutional clients. Source 2026-03-17 Sustainable finance product communications in 2026 continue to focus on data quality, transparency, and transition-risk analytics. Source This section is updated annually to keep the Bloomberg ESG timeline current. Region All regions US Global Type All types Founding Milestone Adoption Governance Showing 6 of 6 events Oct 1981 Founding US # Bloomberg L.P. founded in New York Bloomberg L.P. was founded in 1981 and built financial data infrastructure that later expanded into broad sustainability, climate, and ESG analytics products distributed via terminal and enterprise channels. Bloomberg company overview and history Bloomberg company profile (Encyclopaedia Britannica) Dec 2009 Milestone Global # Bloomberg expands structured ESG data fields in terminal platform Around 2009-2010, Bloomberg materially expanded ESG data collection and standardized fields in its terminal ecosystem, enabling more systematic sustainability screening and portfolio analysis for institutional users. Bloomberg professional sustainable finance solution overview Sep 2015 Adoption Global # Climate and green-finance datasets broaden after Paris era demand shift As climate finance demand accelerated after the Paris Agreement cycle, Bloomberg expanded climate-linked datasets and product integrations used by asset owners, banks, and corporates for reporting and investment analysis. Bloomberg sustainability stories and climate data coverage Nov 2021 Milestone Global # Sustainable finance product suite aligns with expanding disclosure regimes Bloomberg product positioning in the early 2020s increasingly referenced support for mandatory disclosure transitions, including climate metrics, emissions datasets, and transition-risk workflows across regulated markets. Bloomberg Professional \u2014 sustainable finance products Oct 2024 Governance Global # Methodology transparency and data lineage communications expand Bloomberg sustainability communications in 2024-2025 continued emphasizing traceable methodology and data lineage as clients faced tighter audit, assurance, and regulator expectations for ESG-linked datasets and disclosures. Bloomberg company sustainability publications Sep 2025 Adoption Global # Institutional use of Bloomberg ESG and climate analytics remains broad By 2025, Bloomberg ESG and climate analytics remained widely embedded in institutional research and risk workflows, supporting portfolio screening, benchmark construction, and issuer-level disclosure comparisons across sectors. Bloomberg professional sustainable finance platform description Section \u00b7 Tags investor-grade esg-ratings market-data 